# VINW — Vibe Is Not Wish MCP

> **Vibe ≠ Wish.** A Markdown-first, spiral-ascend workflow engine for strict software engineering process control.

## Features

- **7-layer spiral workflow**: L1 需求拆解 → L2 参考文献与方案搜证汇总 → L3 方案细化 → L4 编码实现 → L5 测试验证 → L6 检视清理 → L7 终验
- **Explicit ascend/descend**: Roll back to any baseline and restart a new descent round
- **Markdown-first storage**: Every artifact is a human-readable Markdown file with YAML frontmatter
- **Baseline freeze/rollback**: Each layer can be frozen into read-only baselines; ascending restores them
- **Gate confirmations**: Blocking confirmation items enforce human-in-the-loop at critical transitions
- **Atomic changelog**: Every change, ascent, descent, and baseline is appended to a single append-only log
- **TUI visualization**: Real-time dashboard showing layer states, ascent history, todos, and pending confirmations
- **Cross-harness MCP**: Works with any MCP-compatible agent (Kimi, Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.)

## Quick Start

```bash
# Install
pip install -e .

# Initialize project
vinw init ./projects/my-app --name my-app --desc "My application"

# Start MCP Server (stdio mode for agent harness)
vinw server

# Or start TUI to visualize workflow
vinw tui ./projects/my-app
```

## Layer Structure

Each project is a self-contained directory tree:

```
my-app/
├── .se/
│   ├── manifest.md          # Global state machine
│   ├── changelog.md         # Append-only change log
│   ├── ascensions.md        # Ascent history
│   └── decisions.md         # Cross-layer decisions
├── L1-需求拆解/
│   ├── README.md
│   └── proposals.md
├── L2-参考文献与方案搜证汇总/
│   ├── README.md
│   ├── references.md
│   ├── evidence-matrix.md
│   └── synthesis.md
├── L3-方案细化/
│   ├── README.md
│   ├── design-doc.md
│   └── api-design.md
├── L4-编码实现/
│   ├── README.md
│   ├── implementation.md
│   └── .baseline/
│       └── v001.md
├── L5-测试验证/
│   ├── README.md
│   ├── test-plan.md
│   └── debug-sessions/
├── L6-检视清理/
└── L7-终验/
```

## Spiral Ascend Example

```
descent-1: L1 → L2 → L3 → L4 → L5
                          ↓ Tests reveal design flaw
    se_ascend(L5, L3, "v001", "API contract mismatch")
                          ↓
descent-2:           L3(rollback to v001) → L4 → L5
                                  ↓ Another issue found
    se_ascend(L5, L2, "v001", "Evidence matrix incomplete")
                          ↓
descent-3:      L2 → L3 → L4 → L5 → L6 → L7
```

Each ascent creates an immutable record in `.se/ascensions.md` and increments the descent counter.

## MCP Tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `se_init_project` | Create project with 7-layer structure |
| `se_get_project` | Read full state including layer graph |
| `se_baseline` | Freeze current layer as read-only snapshot |
| `se_ascend` | Rollback to upper layer baseline (new descent round) |
| `se_descend` | Move to lower layer |
| `se_can_descend` | Check if transition is allowed |
| `se_require_confirmation` | Create blocking gate item |
| `se_resolve_confirmation` | Approve/reject/modify gate item |
| `se_store_document` | Write layer document |
| `se_read_document` | Read layer document |
| `se_list_documents` | List layer files |
| `se_log_change` | Atomically log change intent (before modifying) |
| `se_get_changelog` | Read recent changelog entries |
| `se_check_consistency` | Compare design doc with code (LLM / text / AST) |
| `se_store_consistency_report` | Store parsed LLM consistency report |
| `se_search_proposals` | Search proposals across docs (rg / TF-IDF) |
| `se_get_todos` | Scan todos across all layers |
| `se_update_todo` | Update todo list in layer README |
| `se_get_next_steps` | Get recommended actions for current layer |
| `se_list_baselines` | List available baselines |

